  "body": "Reported originally by @chenpighead @ https://github.com/whatwg/compat/issues/66#issuecomment-263093160\r\n\r\n> Here's another issue for webkit-text-stroke-width: from CSS Values and Units Module Level 3, I can't find \"absolute width\" but only \"absolute length\". Since the specified value of -webkit-text-stroke-width is <line-width> and one of the reference could be found in CSS border-width property which uses \"absolute length\" as its computed value, perhaps we should correct \"absolute width\" to be \"absolute length\" or something similar?",
